# Criteria section 7: every declaration is checked as written, used or
# not. From bootstrap/examples/decl-ctx-bracket.moss:
#
# DeclsForm (AUDIT-CHANGES #74; criteria section 7): a context item's
# brackets are read as written: `Nope` is not in scope.
# Verdicts: oracle accepts; native accepts; Audit before accepts; now
# rejects (Brackets: the left side does not resolve). Class B.
#
# The verdicts above predate the self-hosted compiler's check: it now
# rejects this too. The oracle still accepts it (a gap in agreement.rs).
type T;
assume T { fn f(x: T); }
context A = f[Nope = T];
fn main() {}
